Features
User Registration and Authentication

Email and password authentication
Security questions for account recovery
JWT-based session management
Car Listing and Management

List vehicles with detailed information (make, model, year, mileage, etc.)
Upload car images
Set availability calendar and rental pricing
Manage listings (update, delete, mark as unavailable)
Search and Booking

Search cars by location, date, and preferences
Advanced filtering options
Booking system with conflict prevention
Booking management for both owners and renters
Messaging and Communication

Real-time messaging between car owners and renters
Thread-based conversations
Unread message indicators
Car-specific discussions
Notifications

In-app notifications for bookings, messages, and updates
Email notifications for important events
Notification management
Payment System

Simulated payment processing
Transaction history
Security deposit handling
Reviews and Ratings

Rate and review cars and users
Rating aggregation and display
Technology Stack
Frontend

Next.js 14 (App Router)
React 18
TypeScript
Tailwind CSS
Backend

Next.js API Routes
MongoDB
NextAuth.js for authentication
Development Tools

ESLint
Prettier
PostCSS
Design Patterns

=========================================================================================================

DriveShare implements several design patterns to ensure maintainable, scalable code:

Singleton Pattern

Used for authentication session management
Ensures a single instance of critical services

Observer Pattern

Implemented for notifications
Allows multiple subscribers to receive updates

Mediator Pattern

Used for UI component communication
Simplifies interactions between components

Builder Pattern

Applied to car listing creation
Provides flexibility in object construction

Proxy Pattern

Implemented for payment integration
Handles secure communication with payment systems

Chain of Responsibility

Used for password recovery
Creates a secure process using security questions

==========================================================================================================
Getting Started
Prerequisites
Node.js 18.x or higher
npm or yarn
MongoDB database
Installation
Clone the repository:

bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/driveshare.git
cd driveshare
Install dependencies:

bash
npm install
Create a .env.local file in the root directory with the following variables:

MONGODB_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=your_nextauth_secret
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
Note: Replace your_mongodb_connection_string with your own MongoDB URI.

Run the development server:

bash
npm run dev
Open http://localhost:3000 in your browser to see the application.

Database Setup
The application will automatically set up the required collections and indexes when it first connects to your MongoDB database. You can also manually run the setup script:

bash
node scripts/setupDatabase.js

========================================================================================================
API Endpoints
Authentication
POST /api/auth/signup - Register a new user
POST /api/auth/signin - Sign in a user
POST /api/auth/forgotPassword - Recover account with security questions

Cars
GET /api/cars - Get all cars with optional filters
POST /api/cars - Create a new car listing
GET /api/cars/:id - Get a specific car
PUT /api/cars/:id - Update a car listing
DELETE /api/cars/:id - Delete a car listing
PUT /api/cars/:id/availability - Update car availability

Bookings
GET /api/bookings - Get user's bookings
POST /api/bookings - Create a new booking
GET /api/bookings/:id - Get a specific booking
PUT /api/bookings/:id - Update a booking
DELETE /api/bookings/:id - Cancel a booking

Messages
GET /api/messages/threads - Get user's message threads
GET /api/messages/threads/:threadId - Get messages in a thread
POST /api/messages - Send a new message
Notifications
GET /api/notifications - Get user's notifications
PUT /api/notifications/:id - Mark notification as read

Payments
POST /api/payments - Process a payment
GET /api/payments - Get payment history
Authentication
DriveShare uses NextAuth.js for authentication with a custom credentials provider. The authentication flow includes:

User registration with email, password, and security questions
Secure password hashing with bcrypt
JWT-based session management
Password recovery using security questions
The Singleton pattern is implemented for session management to ensure consistent authentication state throughout the application.
